# THE STOCK LOGIC — MARKET FLASH
# ==============================
# Install:  crontab -l > /tmp/ct && cat deploy/market_flash.cron >> /tmp/ct \
#           && crontab /tmp/ct && crontab -l | tail -6
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. engine/market_flash.py was written, tested and merged, and
# then scheduled nowhere. signals.html has been asking for a flash since, finding
# none, and showing "no market note" every session. The code was never the gap.
#
# THE BOX RUNS UTC. IST = UTC + 5:30.
#   13:20 UTC = 18:50 IST
#
# AFTER THE EOD CHAIN, NOT BEFORE. The flash is written from the day's published
# figures -- advance/decline, the regime, the batch counts -- so it has to run
# once 06_push has finished. The chain starts at 18:35 IST; 18:50 gives it fifteen
# minutes and still lands before the 19:10 excursion recorder.
#
# IT CANNOT FAIL CLOSED. The template path is deterministic and takes no network,
# so a missing ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or an unreachable API produces a plain desk note
# rather than nothing. That is the point of having two paths: the page must always
# have a flash and must never show yesterday's prose.
#
# REQUIRES: `market_flash` table (migrations/PENDING_market_flash.sql) and, for the
# written-out path only, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in /etc/atlas.env. Without the table the
# run fails loudly rather than silently; without the key it uses the template and
# says so in the log.
20 13 * * 1-5 cd /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic && set -a && . /etc/atlas.env && set +a && /home/ubuntu/thestocklogic/venv/bin/python -m engine.market_flash >> /home/ubuntu/logs/market_flash.log 2>&1
